From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:48:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 140/151] Find: Replace all replaces empty matches, so ^ and $
 work

Replace all skipped empty matches, so regex `^` with `> ` (prefix every
line) or `$` with `;` changed nothing. It now takes them the way the
regex crate finds them: matches do not overlap and an empty match right
after the previous one is skipped, so `^` and `$` hit each line once and
`x*` in `axxb` does not add a second replacement after `xx`. This holds
for line-by-line and joined queries, and inside "In selection".

Find next, Replace (one) and the count still skip empty matches: there
is nothing to select or show.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

